  "description": "<p>This bug can be seen in the following scenario:</p>\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>After creating, deleting and purging an atomic resource, the path to the purged OCFL object remains, which is invalid.<br/>\n```<br/>\ncurl -i -XPUT -H\"Content-Type: text/turtle\" -d \"&lt;&gt; &lt;<a href=\"http://example.org#title\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://example.org#title</a>&gt; 'a title'\" localhost:8080/rest/container<br/>\ncurl -i localhost:8080/rest/container<br/>\nfind /tmp/fcrepo.ocfl.storage.root.dir -name container<br/>\ncurl -i -XDELETE localhost:8080/rest/container<br/>\ncurl -i localhost:8080/rest/container/fcr:tombstone<br/>\ncurl -i -XDELETE localhost:8080/rest/container/fcr:tombstone<br/>\n// Inspect path returned in the \"find\" command above... notice dangling directory<br/>\n```<br/>\nSee: <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/pull/1687#issuecomment-637912832\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/pull/1687#issuecomment-637912832</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>This issue is also being tracked with: <a href=\"https://github.com/UW-Madison-Library/ocfl-java/issues/8\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/UW-Madison-Library/ocfl-java/issues/8</a></p>",
